1|//! The general-run decider: the terminal ledger-9 relation over the last
2|//! Sherlock IVC node proof (`ivc.rs`), installed as the `acceptRun` verifier
3|//! of `tools/sherlock-sdk/sherlock-run.compact`.
4|//!
5|//! It verifies the node proof under the node key fixed as constants, pins the
6|//! node's `self_vk_repr` lane to that key, folds the carried accumulator,
7|//! resolves every node fixed base and checks the KZG pairing in circuit (the
8|//! residue route of `decider.rs`). It then opens the final state digest as a
9|//! halted state with a `u128` result and exposes the public values
10|//! `[prog_d, init_d, fin_d, n_steps, result]` in the `acceptRun` transcript
11|//! template (`Slot::Value`), with `stmt = H(DOM, prog_d, init_d, fin_d, n, result)`
12|//! and the communication commitment bound to `Poseidon(comm_rand, inputs)`.
13|//!
14|//! The relation is program-independent: one key serves every program; a
15|//! deployment binds its program and initial-state digests through the
16|//! ledger reads in the template.
